 62, "color": "W", "move": "A7", "lead_before": -17.84, "lead_after": -17.89, "points_lost": -0.05, "best": "A7"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Crawling Along the Edge", "summary": "The 12k won when Opus 5.5 resigned. The middle game turned into a swap of first-line and second-line moves, and both sides kept giving points back. White's crawl along the bottom edge had Black ahead by +8.1 after move 16, but Opus 5.5's reply at move 17 gave back 7.9 points. Black was behind from move 19 on, then lost 7.8 more at move 39 and sat at -19.7. The rest was cleanup at around -18 until the resignation.", "moments": [{"turn": 14, "text": "White's F1 was the second step of a first-line crawl along E1, F1, G1. It lost 6.4 points and moved Black's lead from +0.8 to +7.2. The engine would have played C3 instead."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with F2, beside E2 on the second line. The lead fell from +7.2 to +0.4, a loss of 6.7 points. The engine preferred C3, which Opus 5.5 passed over at moves 11, 13, 15 and 17."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "After G1, which lost White 7.6 points, Black was at +8.1. Opus 5.5 pushed on with G2 and dropped to +0.2, a 7.9-point loss and the worst move of its game. The lead had changed hands by the first-line stones, and Black never held it again."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "D4 took the lead from +0.5 to -4.8, a loss of 5.3 points. The engine wanted C4, and White took that point at move 20. It was the first time Black was clearly behind, and it stayed behind from here."}, {"turn": 39, "text": "D5 lost 7.8 points and sent the lead from -12.0 to -19.7. The engine's choice was G8, which White played next at move 40. By then the game was effectively over, and the late moves in the corner and on the left edge hardly moved the number."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints groups with their liberties, count.py only tallies stones and one-colour empty regions for the current position, and the Python edit and cat commands only update notes files (CLAUDE.md, games.md); none of it selects, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}